emrcog-jul2024-02-note099	emrcog-jul2024-02-topic	note	Recurrent vulvovaginal candidiasis (VVC) in pregnancy: management. (Short-answer / learning point — no MCQ options in source.)\n\nAnswer: Clotrimazole pessary 500 mg per vagina: induction once a night for 10–14 nights according to response, then maintenance once a week.\n\nTreatment of VVC in pregnancy is topical: Acute VVC — clotrimazole pessary 500 mg per vagina once a night for up to 7 consecutive nights. Recurrent VVC — induction with clotrimazole pessary 500 mg per vagina once a night for 10–14 nights according to response, then maintenance clotrimazole pessary 500 mg per vagina once a week. (Oral fluconazole regimens used in non-pregnant recurrent VVC are avoided in pregnancy.)	990	2026-07-06 18:38:17.067956
